{"id": "EUVD-2026-93322", "enisaUuid": "5625ade6-d316-3f0f-a740-a77edb0c9b82", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: don't start a ROC while scanning\n\nThe ROC work can be pending when a scan starts (which requires\nROC list to be empty, but that's possible), and then a new ROC\ncan be added to the list and the work will pick it up.\n\nAvoid starting that ROC if a scan made it between things, as\notherwise we'll hit a warning later:\n\n  WARNING: net/mac80211/offchannel.c:404 at ieee80211_start_next_roc+0x256/0x2d0\n  Workqueue: events_unbound cfg80211_wiphy_work\n  Call Trace:\n   __ieee80211_scan_completed+0x4fd/0xe40 net/mac80211/scan.c:537\n   ieee80211_scan_work+0x472/0x1ff0 net/mac80211/scan.c:1193\n   cfg80211_wiphy_work+0x410/0x570 net/wireless/core.c:513", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5dc8ec2f8d1d62914661577c23ec151f5c9734a4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81baab8b645ec532bad2b7a8464191c720ef8fd9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58b806f699052c572dec6cab2c376f884f27e98f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/733f0fde95392ed5f61a4e36aee661ea8d0e8581"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98337", "GHSA-pccj-pwww-vq83"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13bdcb17-8ca7-3ce3-abbc-a6a18fcd245b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.5"}, {"id": "3ec00cd2-e924-3aac-9767-ac6167430a02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "3f0f1c40-0bcb-3aa6-881f-bdb0aa5765b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "4266619d-1ef1-3f22-95e3-25b5c2b8b576", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa016ccd5df89d73483d0d51ee1f692978ccc35 <733f0fde95392ed5f61a4e36aee661ea8d0e8581"}, {"id": "4420f34f-d3a9-3c35-97c5-b30267b64c9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa016ccd5df89d73483d0d51ee1f692978ccc35 <81baab8b645ec532bad2b7a8464191c720ef8fd9"}, {"id": "4d221dcf-c986-389a-8113-9778a66f845a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7fd95a47-e9d1-3de1-9c57-935084777fe9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b3c030e6-ee94-3815-b678-f02804053567", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa016ccd5df89d73483d0d51ee1f692978ccc35 <58b806f699052c572dec6cab2c376f884f27e98f"}, {"id": "d1ecabef-cf3b-3625-9034-39c40f4ad31f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa016ccd5df89d73483d0d51ee1f692978ccc35 <5dc8ec2f8d1d62914661577c23ec151f5c9734a4"}, {"id": "f092f234-b191-372b-8fd9-2f48fccef630", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7cc12f3c-a8ff-396e-9220-43e25b965c84", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}